1
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:20,197
Good morning and welcome to Mario Radio.

2
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:23,560
Today we have a letter from
languishing lonesome boy.

3
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:25,907
Kai, hear me out, he writes.

4
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:29,217
My girlfriend just ghosted
me and I'm super depressed.

5
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,997
I think I may have scared her off
with my out of the blue proposal.

6
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:37,080
And I spent my whole paycheck on
her birthstone engagement ring too.

7
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,297
So you managed to get the
bow and arrow back, huh?

8
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:48,637
Yeah, I found it in Akira's apartment.

9
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,477
He'd been using his stand to help
himself to whatever he wanted.

10
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:56,913
It all totaled up to be 500 million
yen, and the police are already on it.

11
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:00,012
You can try using your stand if you want,

12
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:03,631
but then I'd be forced to hunt
you down and finish you off.

13
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,945
You can't lay a finger
on me while I'm in here!

14
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,885
Chili Pepper has been retired.

15
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,787
Even if he broke out,
I doubt he'd attack us.

16
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,220
Mr. Jotaro?

17
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,797
What about the bow and arrow?

18
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,998
It's going to the Speedwagon
Foundation for analysis.

19
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:25,045
If things go the way I want, we'll
unlock the mystery of stands.

20
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:26,170
Great!

21
00:02:26,253 --> 00:02:27,240
That's fantastic!

22
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,857
After you're done, all
of this will be over!

23
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:32,217
It feels weird celebrating, but woohoo!

24
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,476
We cracked the case!

25
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:36,517
We're still questioning Otoishi
about the other stand users.

26
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,157
There's no way of knowing
how many he awakened.

27
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,720
You'll need to stay on your toes. Got it!

28
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:46,400
The Japanese sure know
how to make a cup of joe!

29
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:48,050
Waitress!

30
00:02:48,133 --> 00:02:49,960
Refill please! Careful!

31
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:51,180
Pay attention!

32
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:53,360
I swear, you're such a klutz.

33
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,659
I can't turn around for one second.

34
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,545
Josuke, it's almost time
for the bus, isn't it?

35
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,570
Oh.

36
00:03:04,653 --> 00:03:05,483
Uh, yeah.

37
00:03:05,566 --> 00:03:06,900
I guess you're right.

38
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,880
Come on, get up. We gotta go.

39
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,037
You think those two are going to be okay?

40
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,300
I'm kind of worried.

41
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:22,020
Holy cannoli!

42
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:24,617
This is the yummiest
cake I've ever tasted!

43
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,759
Waitress, I want some more, please!

44
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:35,320
This is Tomoko.

45
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:36,637
May I ask who's speaking?

46
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,480
Oh, hey, Mom. It's me.

47
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:40,710
Hmm? Josuke?

48
00:03:40,793 --> 00:03:41,818
This is a surprise.

49
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,217
You never call the house.

50
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:44,937
Are you in some kind of trouble?

51
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:47,160
No, uh, why would you think that?

52
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:50,397
Uh, anyway, you're gonna be home
for the rest of the day, right?

53
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,900
Yeah, that's the plan.

54
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,517
Is there something I should know?

55
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,937
No, I just wanted to make sure.

56
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:55,850
Bye!

57
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:57,370
Hey, wait!

58
00:03:57,453 --> 00:03:58,337
What in the world?

59
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:01,773
I swear, that kid had better
not be up to anything fishy.

60
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,240
That was a close one.

61
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,237
I hope Mom doesn't think something's up.

62
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:08,438
This'll be hard enough
without her catching on early.

63
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,631
You've got to be kidding.

64
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:14,094
I told that old geezer to
wait until I was off the phone

65
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,240
Hey, wait up

66
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:25,540
Did you hear me?

67
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,720
I asked you to slow down old man

68
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:32,757
Sorry about that you weren't calling
after me were you? Forget it.

69
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:35,277
We'll never flag down
a cab at this hour so

70
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,357
we're gonna have to
take a bus to my house.

71
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,160
Oh, one more thing.

72
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,929
I know this sounds kind of
pushy, but it has to be said now.

73
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:47,397
Make sure you keep your distance
from mom, and no talking to her.

74
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:51,737
Before we go anywhere, you have to
promise me the terms are non-negotiable.

75
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:55,820
Because if I know my mother, a
simple visit won't be enough for her.

76
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:58,434
She'll become an emotional train wreck.

77
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:02,837
I'm well aware.

78
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:03,980
All right, then.

79
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,230
I promise.

80
00:05:05,313 --> 00:05:09,377
and so we're clear i'm
not i'm gonna be calling

81
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:11,989
you mr joestar the
entire time you're here.

82
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:18,557
look this is awkward but i need to
be as clear as possible strangers

83
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:22,377
that's all the two of us were till
now i know that sounds kind of

84
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:26,637
harsh but it's the truth like it
or not calling you my father just

85
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:32,420
isn't something i'm willing to do
here's the deal after you see mom you

86
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,257
should hurry back to America.

87
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,170
Hmm?

88
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:38,083
Yes, you're right.

89
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:40,340
I completely understand.

90
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,570
Sorry to

91
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,637
trouble you. Shit.

92
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,737
I don't think this could
be any more awkward.

93
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,055
I know the best thing

94
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:54,577
would be to open up, but you can't
force what isn't meant to be.

95
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:56,460
Hey, Mr. Josta - Huh?

96
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:05,140
Excuse me, by any chance, did a
big grandpa-looking guy walk by?

97
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:08,240
He just got on that long-haul bus. Huh?

98
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:12,380
What the hell were you thinking?!

99
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:15,820
Sorry for the hassle.

100
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,777
You said we were going to
get on a bus, so I did.

101
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,837
And it would seem you caught
up not a minute too soon.

102
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:25,177
From the looks of things, we were
just about to merge onto the freeway.

103
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:26,937
I'm starting to think
I should have let that

104
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:29,177
damn bus take you all the way to Hokkaido!

105
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:31,789
At least then I'd -
Oh, damn stomach cramp!

106
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:34,140
I didn't mean to inconvenience you.

107
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,720
Hey, Josuke.

108
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:46,460
Sort of feels like something's pulling
at my pants leg. Yeah? Better be careful.

109
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:50,504
If you drop your guard, it'll drag
you off somewhere and eat you.

110
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:56,750
Huh?

111
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,880
Josuke!

112
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:01,455
Get over here, we've got a stand user!

113
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:04,960
Oh, yeah, you're right.

114
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,460
In fact, there are two users.

115
00:07:07,740 --> 00:07:09,977
And for the record, I'm talking about us.

116
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,380
I'm really thirsty.

117
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,300
White a minute.

118
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,060
These aren't footprints.

119
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:23,850
Hands?

120
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,398
They're handprints!

121
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,360
Oh my god!

122
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,520
The stand just left, Josuke!

123
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:36,637
Did you hear that?

124
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:37,697
It's right there!

125
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:39,368
You can see it in the sand!

126
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:43,832
Yeah, there's no way in hell
I'm letting him meet Mom now.

127
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,273
Not when he's seeing and hearing things.

128
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:49,777
If it weren't for all this
dag-blasted concrete, I could find it!

129
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:50,690
Where'd it go?

130
00:07:50,773 --> 00:07:51,603
It vanished!

131
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:54,420
Why did you disappear? Come back!

132
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:56,810
Great.

133
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,098
This old man is nothing but trouble.

134
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,220
Hermit Purple!

135
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,380
Beat it, mutt! Go on!

136
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,897
Shoo, shoo, get!

137
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:25,780
Hey, uh, am I crazy or is that crying?

138
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,500
Over here, Josuke. Hmm?

139
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,140
It's just a baby.

140
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:34,040
I'm holding a tiny naked baby in my hands.

141
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:37,840
I know it sounds strange,
but it's invisible. What?

142
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,260
It's hard to believe, but you're right.

143
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,020
I can feel its soft skin.

144
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:54,557
How is this even possible
a bonafide invisible baby?

145
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:58,437
From what I can tell it can't
be any older than six months!

146
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:02,357
I want to know how it turned invisible in
the first place and how to get out here?

147
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:05,020
I'm guessing it's the work of a stand but

148
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:08,277
Why on earth would an enemy
stand user turn a baby

149
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:11,077
invisible and where the
hell is this kid's mother?

150
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:13,219
Nothing about this makes any sense.

151
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:20,440
Hey, Josuke, call me crazy, but I
think the baby is the stand user. What?

152
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:23,625
Yeah, it just isn't aware
of its abilities yet.

153
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,657
Whenever it was separated from its mother,

154
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:29,937
the poor little thing must have turned
invisible based on pure instinct.

155
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:34,800
Duress in adults can trigger ulcers,
hair loss, and premature graying.

156
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:39,097
But in the case of this baby,
it's activated its stand powers.

157
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:43,062
If we can find its mother, I think
we might be able to solve this.

158
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,220
Oh, freaking great!

159
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,937
Well, don't just stand there
and make it stop crying!

160
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:50,432
I, uh, don't exactly know how to do that.

161
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:54,677
I have a little bit of experience with
this, but that was a long time ago.

162
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:57,060
There, there, coochie-coochie-goo.

163
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:59,600
Ah, so that's where it is.

164
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,940
Well, is it a boy or a girl?

165
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,680
Yep, this hand has never let me down.

166
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,310
Cairo!

167
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:07,930
Hmm...

168
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:11,360
I'm pleased to say, it's
a girl! Oh, I get it!

169
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:13,157
That's why you had to
use your hand, right?

170
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,652
How else could you tell?

171
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:16,630
Cairo!

172
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:20,569
There's something else
I should know about?

173
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:21,850
Josuke!

174
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,020
Do you have any tissues?

175
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:25,450
Huh?

176
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,030
Cairo!

177
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,840
Th-that nauseating smell!

178
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:33,037
Why the hell is it coming from your hand?

179
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,960
Are you saying she? Yeah!

180
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:38,877
I had no idea she'd even done it
until I got a nose full of nasty,

181
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:42,136
and I just finished scratching
my beard with his hand!

182
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:56,740
Here, I'm returning your manuscript.

183
00:10:57,160 --> 00:11:00,057
I'm looking forward to the
revisions on the second draft.

184
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:00,970
Do your best.

185
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,917
We're stuck with her for now,

186
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,017
so it looks like we'll need to
pick up formula and diapers.

187
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:12,159
And since we don't want her going
au naturel, she needs some clothes.

188
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:16,420
I'm counting on you, Mr. Joestar. What?

189
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,377
You want me to buy everything?

190
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:20,020
Yeah, I can't go in there.

191
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,677
You have any idea how
that would look to people?

192
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:25,857
Somebody could walk by and
catch me buying baby stuff.

193
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:27,357
People would start to talk.

194
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:32,146
They'd see me as some stupid 16-year-old
bad boy who knocked up some poor chick.

195
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:37,357
Okay, I see your point, but I only have
American Traveler's checks at the moment.

196
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,200
I guess I have no choice.

197
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,780
Put whatever you buy on my card.

198
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:43,410
Sorry.

199
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,394
Stay away from all the expensive stuff.

200
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:50,177
I've worked my ass off to build
up that little nest egg, got it?

201
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:51,920
Yeah, yeah, I understand.

202
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,115
Welcome, my good sir.

203
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:57,485
Is there something I can
assist you with today?

204
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,430
Possibly.

205
00:11:58,513 --> 00:12:00,117
Do you have disposable diapers here?

206
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,760
You bet your bonnet we do.

207
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,492
Is this your first time?

208
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,030
Hmm?

209
00:12:05,113 --> 00:12:06,680
Well, yeah, I suppose it is.

210
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,677
These diapers are a cinch to change,

211
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:12,577
even for customers able to live
at home without assistance.

212
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:14,307
You'll rest well with these.

213
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,390
Uh...

214
00:12:16,473 --> 00:12:18,500
no, uh, the diapers aren't for me.

215
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,257
They're for a baby I'm looking after.

216
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:21,170
Goodness!

217
00:12:21,253 --> 00:12:22,560
I'm sorry, how rude of me.

218
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:24,526
Of course they're for a baby.

219
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:29,317
First off, would you
like traditional diapers?

220
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:33,040
Or maybe training pads.
Hmm? Beg your pardon?

221
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,280
As you can see,

222
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:36,797
although traditional
diapers require a cover,

223
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:40,704
they're far more economical and
less wasteful than training pads.

224
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,960
Well, I'm not really sure.

225
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,117
Can I just have this one right here?

226
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,906
And what size would you like?

227
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,140
What do you mean?

228
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,991
How old is the baby, sir?

229
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:53,137
Depending on your child's unique
shape, we have preemies, small,

230
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:54,857
medium, large, and extra large.

231
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:59,317
And not to worry, we have diapers for
boys and girls, so you can't go wrong.

232
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,106
In my day, picking these
out was a lot easier.

233
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:03,870
Let's see.

234
00:13:03,953 --> 00:13:06,157
I know that she's a girl,
and when I held her,

235
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,437
she was about this big,
give or take an inch.

236
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:09,579
When you held her?

237
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,357
I'm afraid I don't follow you.

238
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:15,257
And I don't want to run the risk of you
returning ill-fitting soiled diapers.

239
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:18,237
I'm sure you can understand
the problem with that.

240
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,937
Yeah, completely understand.

241
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:22,137
Guess I'll grab every size you have.

242
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:25,957
In addition to that, I need baby wipes,
instant formula, and baby bottles.

243
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:27,357
Well, then you are in luck.

244
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,997
We carry both glass and
plastic baby bottles.

245
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,777
Glass bottles tend to be
scratch and odor-resistant,

246
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:35,389
but can be heavy for
a baby's arms to hold.

247
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:39,457
Plastic bottles may be light, but
they have a tendency to trap odors.

248
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:41,775
Which of the two would you like today?

249
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:42,990
Let's see.

250
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:46,297
I guess I'll take the one with...

251
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,037
We also carry an assortment
of shapes and designs.

252
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,417
